{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ef48e947a4c70e998653430bb13a9d08a072ac9319e2842cade50995f0f1d32c","digest":{"component_or_area":"test infrastructure / repo-isolation guard","key_entities":["tests/_isolation.py","tests/conftest.py","pytest_sessionfinish","_no_repo_commits","head()","porcelain()","git rev-parse HEAD","git status --porcelain","GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS","subprocess.TimeoutExpired","subprocess.run","_run_process","time.sleep"],"problem_keywords":["repo-isolation","git probe timeout","subprocess hang","pytest_sessionfinish","fixture teardown","monkeypatch contamination"],"propositions":["Read-only Git probes in tests/_isolation.py invoke git status and git rev-parse without timeout, allowing unbounded blocking to keep pytest alive after test completion.","Autouse repo-isolation guard runs during pytest_sessionfinish after [100%] boundary and via _no_repo_commits fixture teardown; blocking Git shims reproduce hangs in real hook call paths.","Test monkeypatches of subprocess.run and time.sleep module contaminate autouse fixture teardown because they dereference mutable shared module attributes before pytest restores them.","Implementation captures real subprocess.run and time.sleep primitives at import time and routes all Git probes through stable bindings with fixed 5-second timeout, explicitly re-raising TimeoutExpired while preserving None for ordinary failures."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787088308388863001,"uuid":"207f1f80-f711-46d7-8fd9-ecd1d2a01cfe"}